      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": [
        {
          "Label": "UNLABELLED",
          "content": "Chronic perineal pain is often a difficult condition to manage. Current treatments include pudendal nerve injections and pudendal nerve release surgery. The obturator internus muscle has a close relationship to the pudendal nerve and might be a potential target for therapeutic intervention."
        },
        {
          "NlmCategory": "CONCLUSIONS",
          "Label": "PERSPECTIVE",
          "content": "A case is presented of refractory perineal pain that was successfully treated by injecting the obturator internus muscle with botulinum toxin A."
        }
      ]},
